From: SaaiOS <os@saaios>
Subject: synaptics td4150: since25 drain leftover ATTN before 0x45

since24: 0x45 still ETIME in RomBoot mode=0x04 with gpio=0 (ATTN
asserted) and irq_en=1. Unread RomBoot IDENTIFY from
sensor_detection blocked command-complete; write_message waited 3s
for a new IRQ. Recovery then sent CMD_GET_ROMBOOT_INFO 0x40.
Probe aborted and freed the IRQ (empty /proc/interrupts).

since25:
- Before 0x45: if ATTN asserted, quiet drain (cap 8, idle-bus stop).
- First 0x45 chunk: if still gpio=0, log leftover attn and drain
  again; fail fast (no 3s wait) if ATTN remains.
- Stop write_message start/spi logs (would wrap on 97k 0x45).
- 0x45 IDENTIFY 0x02 = firmware started, not on-chip skip.
- 0x45 fail: log a reason; one TSP reset retry if reset exists;
  do not unwind IRQ on timeout in FW/RomBoot.
- Log: since25 probe, 0x45 drain, 0x45 chunk 0/N, 0x45 write retval,
  CMD_GET_ROMBOOT_INFO 0x40.

Applies after syna-tcm-hdl-status-idle.patch.

